// @ens-test
// @exit 2
// @stdout-contains PASS first test passes
// @stdout-contains panic: boom
// @stdout-contains crash_test.ens
// @stderr-contains stopped while running 'second test panics'
// @stderr-contains --filter 'second test panics'
// A panic in the second test ends the whole run. The first result is already out, because the
// command passes each line on as its test finishes, and the panic arrives on the same stream in
// the place it happened. The command counted results as they went past, so it names the test.
